  "id": "COMPOUND:24583 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between (20S)-5-Ergostene-3Beta,7Alpha,16Beta,20-Tetrol and VMRC-MELG, mediated through the target SNU-387. This compound appears to act as a common intermediary, with multiple pathways linking it to VMRC-MELG. In Path 1, (20S)-5-Ergostene-3Beta,7Alpha,16Beta,20-Tetrol is directly targeted by SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which ultimately targets VMRC-MELG. In Path 2, (20S)-5-Ergostene-3Beta,7Alpha,16Beta,20-Tetrol is also directly targeted by SNU-387, which is targeted by Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, which again targets VMRC-MELG. Path 3 further confirms this by showing that SNU-387 is targeted by a complex compound, which in turn targets VMRC-MELG. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a common target across all three paths suggests a robust mechanism of action, where (20S)-5-Ergostene-3Beta,7Alpha,16Beta,20-Tetrol may influence VMRC-MELG through SNU-387. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship, where (20S)-5-Ergostene-3Beta,7Alpha,16Beta,20-Tetrol acts as a precursor or modulator of SNU-387, which then influences VMRC-MELG. This mechanism is consistent across the visible paths, reinforcing the integrated explanation of a multi-step interaction between the compound and VMRC-MELG.",
